itter. Won't you help me?"xI've been picking up the trash all morning. It's a lot of work but Pokémon deserve to live in a clean environment.""\PN looked inside the pipe..."2A strange liquid is oozing out of the pipe..."Climb into the pipe?"!\PN climbed into the pipe..."There's nothing there...".You're going to need a shower after this!"kYou've got to help me again! I was robbed by \C[2]Team Magma\C[0]! I have to get the Devon Parts back."BIf I don't... The company's going to be in serious trouble...""Devon Corporation Head Office"'It's a bunch of trash. Pick it up?"You picked up the litter!"JThe Devon Corporation makes all sort of convenient Pokémon products.";I wonder if they had anything to do with DNA Splicers."FNorth: Route 116<br>\nEast: Route 115<br>South: Rustboro City<br>"?The old sailor, Mr. Briney, lives in a cottage by the sea."4He goes for walks in the tunnel every so often."/Have you taken the Pokémon Gym challenge?"yGym Leaders only allow you to use as many Pokémon as they do, so you have to be smart about which one you bring in!"Oh, you there!"DYou're that fantastic trainer who helped me in Petalburg Woods!"<The beach is full of trash. Please help me clean it up."Are you okay?!"YThe Trubbish must've been attracted by your smell from picking up all of this trash!"JWow, the beach looks much nicer now. Thank you so much for your help!"jHere, I want you to have this for helping me out! It was buried under some of the debris you cleaned."(I challenged the Gym Leader, but..."fI thought that bringing in a Grass and Water-type Pokémon would make quick work of Rock types..."_But Fusions make it possible to counter every weakness, you can never know what to expect!"o\PN, you just moved here so you might not know this, but \C[1]Mr. Briney\C[0] was once a revered seafarer."kOh, me? I'm just taking a little break here and enjoying the city before I go on to challenge Roxanne."gI went to the clothing store to find a hat, but I couldn't make up my mind about w