émon Trainer School: Learn everything there is to know about Pokémon fusions!"Yes"NoIu;␀�w[[�"MThere are places that you can't get to without clearing some vegetation."AI think there's a man in this town that's an expert on that."0It's a collection of rare Pokémon fossils!"9Professor Birch's Handy Guide to Pokémon Behaviors:"~When a Pokémon notices a Trainer, its behavior often changes. These behaviors can be classified into several different types."Read more?"�Some curious Pokémon seek to get closer to wandering Trainers without initiating a battle while more shy Pokémon prefer to stay at a safe distance."}More territorial Pokémon such as Poochyena will slowly approach Trainers as a warning and attack them if they don't back up."�Some aggressive Pokémon will chase after Trainers the moment they notice them. Those Pokémon should only be observed at a safe distance."[Of course, every Pokémon is different and some also behave in completely unique ways."3It's a stack of books about Pokémon battling!"qWhenever it stormed, small blue Pokémon with big ears would gather up north to stock up on the electricity."nIt's the work calendar of one of the Devon Corp. employees. It seems like they're in a meeting right now!"DI traded a Pokémon with another trainer I met on my adventure.">But I need to get more Gym Badges for it to listen to me."^I recall seeing an elegant Ghost Pokémon in the fog near the beach up north in my youth."/I wonder if it's still around to this day."7The shelves are stacked with books about Pokémon!"?It's a bunch of code. You can't really make out any of it."GSome Pokémon only come out at night. That's what my teacher said!"hMy dad's a real ace in the Devon Corporation, I'll have you know! It's no wonder I'm an ace myself!"CHere. I'll give you somehing that an Ace Trainer like me uses!"JIf you have a Pokémon hold a Float Stone, its weight will be halved."^It'll probably be a while before you can use something like this as well as I can though.